(17, 'szachowo:2057', 'Capablanca chess (Capablanca chess)-a challenge for the chess player', 'folding-sets', 'sunrise-chess-games', 31.00, 31, 3, 1.1, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "5902560354126", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CH200C"}',
 'Capablanca stupol chess with additional Archbishop and Chancellor pieces. Capablanca chess (or Capablanca chess) is a chess variant invented in the 1920s by world chess champion José Raúl Capablanca. It contains two new pieces and is played on a board of 10×8 or 10x10 squares (variant on offer). Capablanca believed that in a few decades all games between grandmasters would end in draws, which was the main motivation for creating a more complex version of this game. In order to make the game more interesting, Capablanca changed the design of the board and introduced two new pieces into the game: - The archmage moves like a gon and a jumper . - The chancellor moves like a tower and a jumper . The new pieces allow the new creation of new strategies and possibilities that change the game of chess by 180 degrees.'),
