(335, 'szachowo:3519', 'Chessboard No. 5 (unlabelled) redwood/maple (marquetry)', 'wooden-boards', 'sunrise-chess-games', 39.00, 33, 4, 2.4, 48.0, NULL, 48.0,
 '{"ean": "5907311004114", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "D50 REDWOOD W/O"}',
 'Chessboard No. 5, redwood/maple (inlay) , is a tournament-grade chessboard without alphanumeric markings, designed for use with standard-sized, comfortable pieces. The combination of redwood and maple gives it a distinct yet easy-on-the-eye contrast between the squares. The board measures 48 x 48 cm with squares measuring 50 x 50 mm , making it well-suited to medium-sized pieces, including the popular 3.5" size and No. 5 Staunton-style sets, such as the No. 5 Staunton Pieces . It is a good choice for those looking for a full-size board for regular play at home, in a club or during training. Finish and everyday use The dark squares and edges are finished in beautiful redwood , which catches the eye with its warm, deep hue, whilst the light maple squares ensure a clear chessboard layout. The inlaid finish means the surface looks attractive not only during play, but also when the board is left on a table as a permanent fixture. On the underside, there are four pads which improve stability and help protect the tabletop from scratches. This ensures the chessboard sits securely on a desk, table or any other hard, flat surface.'),
