(444, 'szachowo:3433', 'Queen''s Gambit Chess Set, 1957, Ebony-stained Boxwood, 3.75 inches', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 123.00, 0, 5, 1.2, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "5907311004039", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI137 E375"}',
 'A replica of the chess pieces from the World Chess Championship held in Moscow in 1957. Used, amongst other games, in the famous Smyslov–Botvinnik match, and featured in the award-winning series *The Queen’s Gambit*, which is available to watch on Netflix. The favourite chess pieces of Latvian grandmaster Mikhail Tal, often referred to as the ‘Wizard of Riga’. The set comprises 34 chess pieces in both colours (a complete set with additional queens).'),
(445, 'szachowo:3429', 'Queen''s Gambit chess pieces, 1957, Indian acacia, 3.75 inches', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 101.00, 0, 4, 1.2, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "5907311003896", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI137 S375"}',
 'A replica of the chess pieces from the World Chess Championship held in Moscow in 1957. These pieces were used, amongst other games, in the famous Smyslov–Botvinnik match, and featured in the award-winning series *The Queen’s Gambit*, which is available to watch on Netflix. The favourite chess pieces of Latvian grandmaster Mikhail Tal, often referred to as the ‘Wizard of Riga’. The set comprises 34 chess pieces in both colours (a complete set with additional queens). The chessboard shown in the photos is not included in the set.'),
(446, 'szachowo:923', 'Executive Acacia/Boxwood 3,5" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 81.00, 3, 5, 1.1, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 89, "pieces_material": "Acacia/Boxwood", "ean": "5902560355796", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI111 S350"}',
 'This is amazingly well-balanced model of chess pieces. The silhouette of knight should be particularly underlined due to its interesting design. Some people call it ,Laughing Knight’’ as its muzzle is wide open as if it tried to laugh into its ennemies face. All pieces are characteristic because of its slim and detailed design. Black pieces are made of acacia while the white ones are made of boxwood.'),
(447, 'szachowo:878', 'French Staunton Ebonised 3,75" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 71.00, 26, 4, 1.1, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 95, "pieces_material": "Boxwood", "ean": "5902560350425", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI102 E375"}',
 'French Staunton set is a simple and yet elegant variety of popular Staunton chess pieces. All pieces are handmade by Indian craftsmen. Their appearance, especially beautiful polished surface, make them similar to far more expensive models of chess pieces. The robust and solid silhouette of knight is very characteristic for this particular model. The size 3,75'''' correspond to staunton no 6 pieces. All chess pieces are made of the highest quality boxwood (white) and ebonised boxwood (black).'),
(448, 'szachowo:865', 'Zagreb Ebonised chess pieces 3,5''''', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 90.00, 6, 4, 1.1, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 89, "pieces_material": "Boxwood", "ean": "5902560358711", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI103 E350"}',
 'In the 50''s and 60''s of the twentieth century Chess Set "Zagreb" was one of the most popular chess sets that was used in the most important chess tournaments around the world, among others, in Candidates Tournament which took place in 1959, in three cities belonging toYugoslavia - Bled, Belgrade and Zagreb. This beautiful set of chess pieces is provided with two additional queens (white and black). The pieces in this set are very specific -especially King, Queen and Bishop. The Knight is made ​​in the Russian style (note that the head is carved very meticulously its uniqueness being underlined by the horse''s mouth which is closed, slender and bent over a thick neck). Black pieces that we see in the pictures are ebonised . They are made ​​to resemble a real ebony chess pieces.'),
(449, 'szachowo:509', 'German Knight Ebonised 4" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 70.00, 44, 4, 1.4, NULL, NULL, NULL,
