(546, 'szachowo:930', 'Unicorn Redwood 4,25" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 409.00, 0, 5, 2.2, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 110, "ean": "5902560358650", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI115 RED425"}',
 'Another beautiful model from Staunton luxurious pieces collection. One cannot stand indifferently looking on the knight of this model which resembles rather a majestic lion than an ordinary stallion. Compared to other models, this one features marvelously carved knight eyes. They seem to be extremly inteligent and look defiantly at the enemy without any sign of fear. Carefully arranged mane along with the upright ears and a slightly open muzzle make this piece one of the most beautiful at all. Black pieces are made of padauk (Pterocarpus sandalinus) while the white ones are made of boxwood.'),
(547, 'szachowo:945', 'Made In America Knight Ebony 4,25" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 409.00, 0, 3, 2.5, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"pieces_material": "Ebony/Boxwood", "ean": "5902560353860", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI123 H425"}',
 'The present model stands out from the others due to its innovative rook design. The artisans gave up the crenelation on top of it and replaced it by a solid homogeneous fortified tower with a little ball on top. All pieces are really particular, but let us mention the most distinctive ones which are in this case a knight and a king. The last one is definitely unique on account of his cross design which has a tiny hollow circle in the middle. On the other hand, the knight seems proud and solid with its serrated mane. All that makes the design of this set second to none. This interesting model of Staunton chess pieces was surprisingly made in India not America. The black pieces were made of precious and elegant ebony wood while their white equivalents are of boxwood. The chess pieces have been carved very precisely. The care about details strikes at first glance. The height of king amounts to 4 inches which equals to 10,1 cm.'),
(548, 'szachowo:947', 'Parthenon Ebony 4" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 408.00, 0, 5, 2.5, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 101, "pieces_material": "Ebony/Boxwood", "ean": "5902560353846", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI124 H400"}',
 'Expertly crafted chessmen from India. This set can easily compete with the most expensive luxurious models. The black pieces were made of ebony wood while the white ones of boxwood. They are matched with chessboards no 6 or 6+.'),
(549, 'szachowo:936', 'Royal Knight Ebony 4" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 356.00, 0, 4, 2.5, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 101, "pieces_material": "Ebony/Boxwood", "ean": "5902560352313", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI119 H400"}',
 'This model is called Royal Knight as the knight piece resembles one of the stallions from kings’s stable well protected and carefully attended. The mane make us think rather of the nicely combed haircut while the muzzle look like smiling lips. The design of king should be mentioned as well for on its top one can note quite an unusual shape of cross. The whole set is perfectly balanced and should satisfy the most demanding chessmen connoisseurs. All the pieces are made of boxwood and ebony.'),
(550, 'szachowo:937', 'Royal Knight Redwood 4" chess pieces', 'exclusive-pieces', 'sunrise-chess-games', 356.00, 0, 3, 2.5, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"king_height_mm": 101, "pieces_material": "Padauk/Boxwood", "ean": "5902560352320", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "CHI119 RED400"}',
 'This model is called Royal Knight as the knight piece resembles one of the stallions from kings’s stable well protected and carefully attended. The mane make us think rather of the nicely combed haircut while the muzzle look like smiling lips. The design of king should be mentioned as well for on its top one can note quite an unusual shape of cross. The whole set is perfectly balanced and should satisfy the most demanding chessmen connoisseurs. The black pieces are made of red padauk (Pterocarpus sandalinus) thanks to which its appearence is absolutely fascinating.'),
