(1066, 'szachowo:689', 'Yearbook 117 hardcover: Chess Opening News (HC)', 'new-in-chess-books', 'new-in-chess', 35.00, 0, 4, 0.62, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "9789056915919", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "9789056915919"}',
 'Forum The Forum Section has a highly interesting discussion on the book The Lazy Man’s Sicilian with contributions by Ashot Nadanian and Dvoretsky. Other contributions by, among others, Bogdan Lalic and Viacheslav Zakhartsov. Columns Joel Benjamin continues his new column Repertoire Building with Benjamin writing about a consistent and non-labour-intensive approach to Sicilians with 2…Nc6. In Kuzmin’s Harvest, Alexey Kuzmin takes a look at important opening developments in the World Cup in Baku. Preview This Yearbook has a preview of the new version of A Chess Opening Repertoire for Blitz and Rapid, written by the well-known grandmaster Evgeny Sveshnikov and his son Vladimir. Reviews Glenn Flear reviews Junior Tay’s The Old Indian: move by move, Simon Williams’ the killer Dutch, The Lazy Man’s Sicilian by Valeri Bronznik and Steve Giddins, and Boris Avrukh’s new Grandmaster Repertoire installment, no. 1A: 1.d4 – The Catalan.'),
(1067, 'szachowo:691', 'Yearbook 118: Chess Opening News (HC)', 'new-in-chess-books', 'new-in-chess', 35.00, 0, 4, 0.62, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "9789056916404", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "9789056916404"}',
 'Forum The Forum Section contains a quite vehement discussion on the right to give your name to an opening variation, the announcement of the winner of the Novelty of the Year 2015 contest, as well as theoretical contributions by, among others, Bogdan Lalic, Luis Rodi and José Vilela. Moreover, we are preparing a very special surprise for you! Columns In his column Repertoire Building with Benjamin, the American GM starts an intriguing discussion of isolated queen’s pawn positions in different openings. In Kuzmin’s Harvest, Alexey Kuzmin takes a look at what the world top has cooked up opening-wise for the annual Tata Steel event. Reviews Glenn Flear reviews Grandmaster Repertoire: The Dragon, Volumes 1 and 2, by Gawain Jones, Understanding the Queen’s Gambit Accepted by Alexander Delchev and Semko Semkov, David Smerdon’s acclaimed The Scandinavian, as well as Alexey Bezgodov’s latest opening book called The Double Queen’s Gambit.'),
(1068, 'szachowo:694', 'Yearbook 119: Chess Opening News', 'new-in-chess-books', 'new-in-chess', 30.00, 0, 4, 0.48, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "9789056916411", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "9789056916411"}',
 'Forum The Forum Section features new theoretical contributions by, among others, Bogdan Lalic and Vishnu Prasanna. Columns In his column Repertoire Building with Benjamin, the American GM continues his treatment of the highly important position type with an isolated queen’s pawn. In Kuzmin’s Harvest, Alexey Kuzmin highlights the most important opening novelties in the Candidates’ Tournament in Moscow. Reviews Glenn Flear reviews three repertoire books: The Open Games with Black by Martin Lokander (Everyman), Playing 1.e4 e5 – A Classical Repertoire (Nikolaos Ntirlis, Quality), and A Chess Opening Repertoire for Blitz and Rapid by Evgeny Sveshnikov and his son Vladimir (New In Chess). Also, two new books on the Scandinavian Defence: Sergey Kasparov’s Understanding the Scandinavian (Gambit) and Vassilios Kotronias’ The Safest Scandinavian (Chess Stars).'),
