(1461, 'szachowo:556', 'Size No 5+ (without notation) walnut/maple', 'more-chess-books', 'quality-chess', 30.00, 0, 4, 0.86, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "9781784832742", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "9781784832742"}',
 'This 52x52cm veneer chessboard has been crafted from maple and walnut. This fine chess board has a square size of 55mm and it fits to our medium and larger chessmen with a King height of 90 and 98mm. Chess pieces from picture are not the part of the offer and You can buy it separately in chess pieces section.'),
(1462, 'szachowo:2333', 'Mastery A. Yusupov all 3 books', 'more-chess-books', 'quality-chess', 76.00, 0, 5, 0.5, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "5907311002981", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "5907311002981"}',
 'Throughout the 10 book series, Yusupov guides the reader towards a higher chess understanding using carefully selected positions and advice. To make sure that this new knowledge sticks, it is then tested by a selection of puzzles. The various topics – Tactics, Strategy, Positional Play, the Endgame, Calculating Variations, Openings and so on – are spread evenly over the ten volumes, giving the readers the chance to improve every area as they work through the books. Mastery (also known as ‘the green books’) is the third level in Yusupov’s 3 levels, and builds on the material introduced in the Fundamentals and Beyond the basics books from the first and second levels. The books from this bundle: Yusupov Build Up Your Chess: Mastery 3 is the first volume in Yusupov’s Mastery series. Yusupov guides the reader towards a higher chess understanding using carefully selected positions and advice. To make sure that this new knowledge sticks, it is then tested by a selection of puzzles. Yusupov Boost Your Chess: Mastery 3 is the second book in Yusupov’s Mastery series, continuing on from the material covered in the first book.'),
(1463, 'szachowo:2330', 'Chess Camp Volume 1 - 7', 'more-chess-books', 'quality-chess', 73.00, 0, 3, 0.56, NULL, NULL, NULL,
 '{"ean": "5907311002936", "supplier": "Sunrise Chess & Games", "supplier_sku": "2000010029365"}',
 'M ove, Attack, and Captur e Simple Checkmates Checkmates with Many Pieces Elementary Endgame s Two-Move Checkmates Tactics in Attack and Defense Opening Tactics Chess Camp is a new training system for beginning chessplayers, and for the parents and coaches who teach them. Starting with simple problems to illustrate key concepts, and then progressing to more complex positions, the student will learn by doing, methodically integrating new information with previous knowledge while building effective thinking habits at the board. About the Author Igor Sukhin has been using the game of chess for more than two decades to teach children. His books have been selected repeatedly as recommended reading by the Russian Department of Education. The author of the acclaimed children’s chess book Gary’s Adventures in Chess Country (also published by Mongoose Press), Sukhin has written more than 100 titles, with over a million copies currently in print.'),
